WEBVTT

00:00:02.715 --> 00:00:06.521
Spec Studio is a Mac app for spec-driven development with Claude Code.

00:00:06.521 --> 00:00:11.631
You describe a change, and one Claude session takes it from a spec to reviewed pull requests.

00:00:18.412 --> 00:00:19.926
Make a spec in any repo.

00:00:19.926 --> 00:00:23.585
Give it a title and say what a user sees when it is done.

00:00:23.585 --> 00:00:31.787
In Autopilot, Claude writes the spec and the plan, builds the change and opens a draft pull request, with no question in between.

00:00:37.731 --> 00:00:40.094
Every spec moves through five stages.

00:00:40.094 --> 00:00:49.225
The reader shows each document while Claude writes it: the spec with its scenarios, the plan, the build with its pull request, and the review.

00:00:49.225 --> 00:00:52.034
The strip at the top says whose turn it is.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:03.971
In Check, a self review reads the pull request with parallel finders, and three verifiers vote on each finding.

00:01:03.971 --> 00:01:05.717
Here it found two problems.

00:01:05.717 --> 00:01:09.021
Claude fixed both, and a second round found nothing.

00:01:09.021 --> 00:01:10.518
Then it is over to you.

00:01:16.369 --> 00:01:17.497
Away from the Mac?

00:01:17.497 --> 00:01:20.503
The relay is a remote MCP server that you host.

00:01:20.503 --> 00:01:27.143
Claude AI, or Claude Code on another computer, can list your specs, read them, and send a spec a message.

00:01:33.273 --> 00:01:36.700
The message reaches the spec's session as a message from Claude AI.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:40.843
Claude makes the change and answers, and the answer goes back through the relay.

00:01:48.969 --> 00:01:50.999
Later, ask again from anywhere.

00:01:50.999 --> 00:01:56.957
Claude reads the spec through the relay, with its stage, its pull request, and the answer.

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:16.309
The relay keeps its copy of each spec in a Temporal namespace: Temporal Cloud, or a Temporal that you host.

00:02:16.309 --> 00:02:20.702
Attachments go to any S3 compatible bucket, such as R2, S3 or MinIO.

00:02:20.702 --> 00:02:23.567
Run it with Docker Compose, Helm, or Docker.

00:02:27.607 --> 00:02:29.299
Install Spec Studio with Homebrew.

00:02:29.299 --> 00:02:33.180
The guides on the site take you through the app, the relay, and its backends.
